# Local state: the JSON config carries both keys and the database carries
# encrypted mail passwords. Neither belongs anywhere near version control.
dev_config/
# Anchored with a leading slash so they mean "the compiled binary in the repo
# root" and nothing else. Unanchored, "mailctl" matches ANY path segment of
# that name -- which silently excluded src/cmd/mailctl/ entirely, so the tool's
# source was never committed at all. A gitignore that hides source is invisible
# until the day somebody clones the repository and the tool is not in it.
/starry_go_mail
/mailctl
/funcsdoc
# The compiled-in pepper. Changing it makes every stored mail password and
# TOTP secret undecryptable, so it is kept out of version control and backed up
# with the config -- not regenerated.
pepper.txt

# Editor scratch. A swap file was committed once and then kept turning up as a
# deletion whenever somebody closed the editor -- it is the editor's state, not
# the project's.
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Compose reads PEPPER from the environment, and a .env file beside
# docker-compose.yaml is the obvious place to put it. It is the one value that
# must never be committed: see Docker.How.To.
.env

# A personal helper, one line: "claude --resume <session-id>". It was committed
# once by accident and untracked again in e8bd4b6; this keeps a stray `git add`
# from putting it back.
st_claude

# Generated by build.sh, every build, from the file beside them. Committing them
# put a pair of binary blobs in the diff for every stylesheet edit, and a
# reviewer cannot read either one.
#
# Losing them is not a broken build: compress.go gzips responses at level 5 per
# request, so a binary built without them still serves compressed assets.
# What is lost is brotli -- the standard library has no encoder, so it can only
# come from the build -- and the higher gzip level, computed once instead of on
# every request. Measured on mail.min.css: 8922 bytes brotli, 10027 gzip -9,
# 10325 from the runtime compressor.
#
# Nothing warns about it, so: run ./build.sh, which writes them before the
# //go:embed and keeps them matching the source they came from.
src/static/*.brotli
src/static/*.gz
